- op: discuss  # 2d11
  at: '2026-08-21T00:31:11Z'  # 2d11
  by: agent  # 2d11
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2d11
  clock: 15  # 2d11
  nonce: 2d11  # 2d11
  message: "CLASS NOT DRAINED -- two further instances found 2026-08-20, and the reason they were invisible is now fixed. This item is pending_validation on the premise that every fs-write primitive on a claimed entry point routes through a safety_zones wrapper. Two did not: gitleaks.py:210 and the rust-analyzer probe at graceful_degrade.py:159 both called tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() directly, while runtime-cli-no-host-fs and install-gitleaks-no-host-fs assert that ALL writes go through the wrappers. WHY THEY NEVER SURFACED, which is the part worth keeping: this item's statement enumerates the primitives as write_text / mkdir / unlink / chmod / copy2 / rmtree / replace. TemporaryDirectory is none of those -- it is CONSTRUCTOR-shaped, and until INV-lalad the taint walk could not traverse construction edges at all (instantiates was absent from TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES), so the two call sites could not surface as raw host_fs flows no matter how carefully anyone looked. The drain looked complete because the instrument could not see the residue. An enumerated list of primitives is only ever as complete as the analysis that would notice a missing one. FIXED in the same PR (a134baac5c): a tmp_artifact_dir() context-manager wrapper joins the tmp_artifact zone and both sites route through it; check-self-claims returns to 18 unchanged verdicts, restored by fixing the code rather than re-recording the snapshot. NOT reopening this item -- its own filed repro concerned Path.mkdir in build_grammars + gitleaks and that fix stands. Recording so that its eventual bakeoff validation is judged against a statement whose primitive enumeration is now known to be non-exhaustive, and so nobody reads its pending_validation as 'the class is closed pending confirmation'."  # 2d11
